      {
        "id": 151600,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-12-22T14:19:04.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Things we find out in Villains &nbsp;<strong>Copy this quick before a mod deletes it!</strong></p><p>Legacy didn't like peas until he was 22.</p><p>Unity has a pet Raptor Bot that she won't take into battle, she calls it Charlie, it loves to hide in Bunkers unused suits.</p><p>La Capitan for a short while went under the title Maria the Mariner, which she ditched after they traded Ken Griffey Jr.</p><p>Miss Information similarly played around with the name Innacurate Data, but no one took her menacing letters to the editor seriously.</p><p>Baron Blade keeps trying to destroy the Freedom Tower because, \"It looks hideous, it doesn't fit the skyline at all, I mean doesn't Megalopolis have a city planners office?\"</p><p>The Chairman disagrees with this assessment, and is actually a big fan of the tower's design.</p><p>Chrono Ranger isn't actually a time-traveller, he made up the story and pretends to talk to Con all the time to hide that he's listenning to Smooth Jazz during battles.</p><p>Expatriette doesn't like kittens, but she thinks Turtles are the cutest things ever.</p><p>Tachyon may be the fastest woman on Earth, but she's never placed higher than third at interplanetaries.</p><p>The government continues to refuse permits for Tachyon to build a big ramp that would let her build up speed and \"Run to Mars\", a decision Tachyon claims could save weeks off the time it takes to communicate with Wagner Mars Base.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:30:30.089Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
